<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fernán González of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 910–970</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fernán González was Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from about 931 to 970. He united the counties of Castile, Álava and Lantarón under his rule and made Castile largely autonomous from the kings of León. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, took part in León's succession disputes and made the countship hereditary. Later epic poetry made him a Castilian hero.</p></div>
